From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:05:40 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 33/35] Plutonium: the dock's slot editor, and sites' own icons

A right click on a dock button (or a click on an empty one) opens a popover
above the dock with the slot's settings: what it opens (the terminal, an app
from a filterable list of the installed ones, or a site's address and the
prefix its tabs start with), its name, where it's kept (this thread, this
project, everywhere, with what that means), its layout (and this thread's
own, with a way back to the slot's), and Clear. Changes apply as they're
made. "Use the panel's tab" fills it from what the panel shows.

A site's button shows the site's icon: an open tab's, else the one T3
remembers, else the one captured when it was put in the dock, else the
site's own /favicon.ico (GitHub's drawn for the theme, so it shows on a
dark sidebar). No third-party favicon service.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
